Results FX sampler (JOED-63)

The read-only sampler uses its dedicated paper client 709 to request
reqAccountUpdatesMulti(id, ACCOUNT, "", true). It collects ExchangeRate values
for the configured account until accountUpdateMultiEnd and always cancels the
request before disconnecting. It makes no FX market-data request. EUR must be
exactly 1 to prove an EUR base; the positive USD decimal rate is padded or
rounded half-even to eight decimal places using BigInt.

IB updates account values periodically. This is IB's valuation rate as received
at sampleAt, not a simultaneous executable FX quote. sampleAt records receipt
of the USD account value, before accountUpdateMultiEnd. The producer carries
that timestamp unchanged as observedAt.

staleFx: true and integer staleSeconds appear together once the rate string
has stayed identical for at least 1800 seconds (30 minutes), measured from the
earliest sample in the contiguous identical run of that New York day's samples
to the new RTH or close sample's sampleAt, rounded down to seconds. A different
rate resets the run; failed attempts do not change it. Below 1800 seconds both
keys are absent. This is informational: the rate is still used for conversion.

New samples carry source "ib-account-exchange-rate". The producer labels their
conversions "ib-account-fx-close" or "ib-account-fx-rth". Historical samples
without source retain "ib-fx-close" or "ib-fx-rth". A frozen 16:05 New York
close wins for its day; an RTH sample expires after 30 minutes. A fill's own
closeFx keeps its existing 60-second freshness requirement.

Slots, the 15-minute gap, unconditional close, one attempt per bucket, timeout,
reserved request IDs, retention and FX-SAMPLER-OFF are unchanged. Failed IB
requests may record an integer code with the existing reason. Broker messages
and account IDs are never logged or persisted by the sampler. Old state files
without source or code remain readable; unknown sample sources fail closed.
